  "rationale": "Without mitigations rce_achieved is reachable. trust_url_codebase is already false, so load_class_via_reference is blocked, but the gadget route works: inject_jndi_string -> trigger_jndi_lookup -> resolve_to_attacker -> return_malicious_reference -> load_class_via_gadget -> execute_payload. Every step of this single remaining path is required, so one mitigation that breaks any step is enough. Examples: formatMsgNoLookups (message_lookups false blocks trigger_jndi_lookup), disable_jndi, remove_jndi_class, block_egress, input_validation or remove_gadget. I read each mitigation as turning off its matching condition, which is the evident intent even though the prose says it makes the constant true. trust_url_codebase_false alone would not help, since that condition is already false. Zero mitigations is not enough because the attack succeeds with none deployed, so the minimum is 1."
